<title>JAPAN: Japan LDP may start mulling stocks tax in Feb - Jiji.</title>
<headline>Japan LDP may start mulling stocks tax in Feb - Jiji.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party (LDP) may start considering ways to abolish a tax on securities transactions from February, Jiji news agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>Jiji quoted senior LDP member Michio Ochi as telling reporters he hoped the Finance Ministry would come up with measures to cope with the stock market plunge in addition to long-term reforms planned for the share market.</p>
<p>&quot;After the supplementary budget is approved, our Tax System Research Commission will start meeting as early as February. We would like to review the securities transaction tax as well as financial service taxes,&quot; Ochi was quoted as saying.</p>
</text>
